#. translators: Notice at the top of the WPML Languages editor, shown when changes from an earlier visit were never saved.
msgid "You have unsaved language changes from a previous session."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Button label in the WPML Languages editor that brings back the unsaved changes from an earlier visit. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Restore changes"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Button label in the WPML Languages editor that throws the unsaved changes away. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Discard"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Notice at the top of the WPML Languages editor, shown when changes from an earlier visit could not be brought back because the site's languages have changed since.
msgid "Unsaved language changes from a previous session could not be restored, because the site’s languages changed after they were made. Those changes were discarded."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Button label in the WPML Languages editor that closes the notice about discarded unsaved changes. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Dismiss"
msgstr ""

msgid "Impact on existing content"
msgstr ""

msgid "Checking which content will be affected…"
msgstr ""

msgid "We couldn’t estimate the impact. You can still apply the change; content will be updated during the save."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Button label that runs the action again after it failed, used across WPML's screens. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Try again"
msgstr ""

msgid "No existing content needs updating."
msgstr ""

#. translators: One item of the list of what a language change will touch, in the WPML Languages editor. %d: the number of posts.
#, js-format
msgid "%d post will be updated."
msgid_plural "%d posts will be updated."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: One item of the list of what a language change will touch, in the WPML Languages editor. %d: the number of links.
#, js-format
msgid "%d link will be adjusted."
msgid_plural "%d links will be adjusted."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: One item of the list of what a language change will touch, in the WPML Languages editor. %d: the number of translated strings that get a new key.
#, js-format
msgid "%d translated string will be re-keyed."
msgid_plural "%d translated strings will be re-keyed."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Heading of the dialog that finishes a language change in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language with its new country, e.g. "Spanish (Venezuela)". Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Finish the change to %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Heading of the list of things WPML changes by itself, in the dialog that finishes a language change in the WPML Languages editor.
msgid "What changes automatically"
msgstr ""

#. translators: One item of that list in the WPML Languages editor. %s: a country name, or the words "International" or "Regional".
#, js-format
msgid "The language’s country becomes %s."
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatic translation will be re-mapped to the new regional variant. Existing translations stay as they are."
msgstr ""

msgid "Automatic translation will now target the new regional variant. Existing translations stay as they are."
msgstr ""

#. translators: One item of that list in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the new hreflang tag, e.g. "es-VE". "hreflang" is the name of an HTML attribute; keep it.
#, js-format
msgid "The hreflang tag becomes %s."
msgstr ""

msgid "Also update these?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Heading over the choice, in the dialog that finishes a language change in the WPML Languages editor, that can break existing links (the change of the language code in URLs). It is shown apart from the harmless choices and is off unless ticked.
msgid "Riskier change"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Button label that closes a dialog or a box without applying anything, used across WPML's screens. Verb, imperative, not the status of a cancelled job.
msgid "Cancel"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Button label that puts the choices in a dialog into effect, used across WPML's screens. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Apply"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Sentence added to a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language being added, e.g. "German (Austria)" or "Italian" — it follows "in", so the sentence needs no article before the name.
#, js-format
msgid "Anything whose translation group already has a version in %s stays where it is."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %1$d: how many pages there are, %2$s: the name of the language that was removed, e.g. "German".
#, js-format
msgid "You have %1$d %2$s page from a language you removed. Bring it here?"
msgid_plural "You have %1$d %2$s pages from a language you removed. Bring them here?"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Label of the tick box that acknowledges a language change in the WPML Languages editor. %1$s: the language that was removed, %2$s: the language being added.
#, js-format
msgid "I understand these items are not %1$s and will be re-labelled as %2$s."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language being added, e.g. "German (Austria)".
#, js-format
msgid "Re-labels them as %s, keeping their connections to your other languages."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Heading of the dialog that offers to move content from a removed language, in the WPML Languages editor.
msgid "Content from a language you removed"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Heading above the list of choices in that dialog, in the WPML Languages editor. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Choose what to bring here"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Button label that puts the ticked changes into effect, in the WPML Languages editor. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Apply changes"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Note at the bottom of that dialog in the WPML Languages editor. "Save" is the label of the editor's own save button; translate it the same way there.
msgid "These changes are applied when you click Save."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %1$s: the WordPress locale used now, e.g. "es_CO", %2$s: the new one, e.g. "es_VE". "WordPress locale" is the name of a setting; the codes themselves are never translated.
#, js-format
msgid "Change the WordPress locale %1$s → %2$s"
msgstr ""

msgid "WordPress uses this to load admin language packs and plugin / theme translations."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Why a choice cannot be ticked, in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the name of the language that already has this setting.
#, js-format
msgid "Already used by %s."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %1$s: the code used in URLs now, e.g. "/es/", %2$s: the new one, e.g. "/es-ve/". The codes themselves are never translated.
#, js-format
msgid "Change the language code in URLs %1$s → %2$s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the code used in URLs now, e.g. "/es/". "404" is the browser's not-found error.
#, js-format
msgid "Renames the language code. Existing %s URLs in search engines, bookmarks and external links become 404s unless redirects are set up."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the name of the country, or of the language, whose flag is offered. Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Use the flag of %s"
msgstr ""

msgid "You picked the current flag yourself, so WPML keeps it unless you ask."
msgstr ""

msgid "The flag shown in language switchers and in the admin."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %1$s: the language's name now, %2$s: its new name. Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Rename the language %1$s → %2$s"
msgstr ""

msgid "Updates the name in every language of the admin. Labels you edited yourself are kept."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %1$s: the hreflang tag used now, %2$s: the new one. "hreflang" is the name of an HTML attribute and the tags themselves are never translated. Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Change the hreflang tag %1$s → %2$s"
msgstr ""

msgid "You customised this tag, so WPML keeps it unless you ask. Search engines read it to serve the right regional version."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Heading of the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language name, e.g. "German".
#, js-format
msgid "What should happen to %s?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Pick the outcome you want. Nothing happens until you confirm below."
msgstr ""

msgid "Checking for translated content…"
msgstr ""

msgid "What should happen to this language"
msgstr ""

msgid "Which content types"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of a tick box that includes one group of content, in the dialog that removes a language. %1$s: the group's name, e.g. "Pages and posts", %2$d: how many items it holds.
#, js-format
msgid "%1$s — %2$d item"
msgid_plural "%1$s — %2$d items"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Name of a group of content in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. Plural nouns.
msgid "Pages and posts"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Name of a group of content in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. It means WooCommerce products. Plural noun.
msgid "Products"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Name of a group of content in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. Plural nouns.
msgid "Categories and tags"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Name of a group of content in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. It means the pictures in the media library. Plural noun.
msgid "Images"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Name of a group of content in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. It means the site's navigation menus. Plural noun.
msgid "Menus"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Radio button in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor; "them" is the content of that language. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Delete them permanently now — this cannot be undone"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Note under the radio buttons in the dialog that removes a language; "those" is the categories, tags and menus just named.
msgid "Categories, tags and menus have no WordPress Trash, so those are deleted right away either way."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Statement in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the other languages of the site, e.g. "English, French". The words in quotation marks are the name of a WPML setting; translate them the way that setting is translated.
#, js-format
msgid "Your site’s setting “when deleting a post, delete its translations too” is on. We will not apply it here, so nothing in %s is deleted."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Separator between names in a list, as in "German, Spanish and French". Keep the trailing space.
msgid ", "
msgstr ""

#. translators: Stands in for the list of language names in the sentence above when the site has none to name. It sits inside that sentence, so it starts in lower case.
msgid "your other languages"
msgstr ""

#. translators: One item of the list of what removing a language does, in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language name, e.g. "German".
#, js-format
msgid "%s’s string translations are deleted with it."
msgstr ""

#. translators: One item of the list of what removing a language does, in the WPML Languages editor; "Its" is that language's.
msgid "Its queued translation jobs are cancelled without charge; any already in progress are stopped, and the words already sent are still charged."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of the dropdown that picks where the content goes, in the dialog that removes a language. The dropdown finishes the sentence, so there is no full stop.
msgid "Move this content into"
msgstr ""

#. translators: First option of the dropdown that picks where the content goes, in the dialog that removes a language. Verb, imperative; keep the ellipsis.
msgid "Choose a language…"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Heading of the group of options in that dropdown that are the same language in another country, e.g. Spanish (Mexico) under Spanish.
msgid "Same language"
msgstr ""

msgid "A different language"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of the tick box that acknowledges the move, in the dialog that removes a language. %s: the language name, e.g. "German".
#, js-format
msgid "I understand these items are not %s and will be re-labelled as the language I pick."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Note under the move options in the dialog that removes a language. %s: the language name, e.g. "German".
#, js-format
msgid "%s is taken off the site when you save, and its content is moved straight after — nothing is deleted either way."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Error in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language name, e.g. "German".
#, js-format
msgid "WPML could not stop translating into %s. Nothing was changed — try again, or pick another goal."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Button label that lists the items before anything happens, in the dialog that removes a language. %d: how many items would be listed. Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Review %d item"
msgid_plural "Review %d items"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Label of the confirming button in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language name, e.g. "German". Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Stop translating into %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of the confirming button in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. %1$d: how many items move, %2$s: the language they move into. Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Move %1$d item into %2$s"
msgid_plural "Move %1$d items into %2$s"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Label of the confirming button in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. %d: how many items move. Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Move %d item"
msgid_plural "Move %d items"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Label of the confirming button in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. %d: how many items go to the Trash. Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Move %d item to the Trash"
msgid_plural "Move %d items to the Trash"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Label of the confirming button in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. %d: how many items are deleted for good. Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Delete %d item permanently"
msgid_plural "Delete %d items permanently"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

msgid "Remove language — nothing is deleted"
msgstr ""

msgid "What would be removed"
msgstr ""

msgid "Hide the list"
msgstr ""

msgid "Reading the list…"
msgstr ""

msgid "We couldn’t read the list of items. The counts above still stand, and you can go ahead or close this dialog."
msgstr ""

#. translators: One row of the list of content in the WPML Languages editor. %1$s: the item's title, %2$s: the name of its content type, %3$d: its number. Keep the # before the number.
#, js-format
msgid "%1$s — %2$s (#%3$d)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Shown in place of the list of content in the WPML Languages editor when nothing is ticked.
msgid "Nothing is selected right now."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Range line under the list of content in the WPML Languages editor. %1$d: the first row shown, %2$d: the last row shown, %3$d: how many rows there are altogether.
#, js-format
msgid "Showing %1$d–%2$d of %3$d item"
msgid_plural "Showing %1$d–%2$d of %3$d items"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Used on WPML's paged lists for the control that goes back one page: the visible button label, and the accessible label (screen readers) of the back arrow.
msgid "Previous"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Used on WPML's paged lists for the control that goes forward one page: the visible button label, and the accessible label (screen readers) of the forward arrow.
msgid "Next"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Result line in the WPML Languages editor after a language was removed. %s: the language name, e.g. "German". "Removed languages" is the name of a panel on the same screen; translate it the same way there.
#, js-format
msgid "%s is off your site, but its content could not be moved. Nothing was deleted — the content is listed under Removed languages, where you can move it from."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Used in two places on WPML's screens: the heading of the dialog that reports a finished action, and the marker on a step that is already done. It means "finished", not a command.
msgid "Done"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Result line in the WPML Languages editor after translation into a language was stopped. %s: the language name, e.g. "German".
#, js-format
msgid "%s stays on your site. Its pages keep their addresses and their search rankings, and the language switcher keeps offering it."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Result line in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language name, e.g. "German". "Resume translating" is a control on the same screen; translate it the same way there.
#, js-format
msgid "WPML has stopped creating new %s translations. To start again, use “Resume translating” on the language’s row."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Result line in the WPML Languages editor after a language was taken off the site. %1$s: the language name, %2$s: the site's default language.
#, js-format
msgid "%1$s is off your site. Nothing was deleted: its addresses now redirect to your %2$s pages, and every item it holds is still in your database and in your admin lists."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Result line in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language name, e.g. "German". "Put back" and "Removed languages" are a control and a panel on the same screen; translate them the same way there.
#, js-format
msgid "To bring %s back, add it again — or use “Put back” under Removed languages, below."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Result line in the WPML Languages editor, for a language the site owner created themselves. %s: the language name, e.g. "Aussie English". "custom language" is the editor's own wording for a language the user adds by hand; translate it the same way there.
#, js-format
msgid "To bring %s back, add it again as a custom language with the same code — its content is still here."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Result line in the WPML Languages editor, for a language that has no country on record. %s: the language name, e.g. "German". "language picker" is the search-and-add box on the same screen; translate it the same way there.
#, js-format
msgid "To bring %s back, add it again from the language picker — it asks which country the content belongs to, and the content is still here."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Result line in the WPML Languages editor after content went to the Trash; "They" is that content. %s: the date it is emptied, in the site's own format, e.g. "4/12/2026".
#, js-format
msgid "They stay in your Trash until %s."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Result line in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language name, e.g. "German".
#, js-format
msgid "The deletion of %s’s content finished. WPML could not read back a record of what it removed."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Button label that closes a dialog, used across WPML's screens. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Close"
msgstr ""

msgid "Unavailable until WPML can count this language’s content."
msgstr ""

msgid "If your site uses one domain per language, that language’s domain is not redirected: while it still points at this site it answers in your site’s default language at the same addresses."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under the choice that deletes a language's content, in the WPML Languages editor.
msgid "The listed items are removed, along with their translation records, their string translations and their translation jobs."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under the choice that deletes a language's content, in the WPML Languages editor. %d: how many translation jobs go with it.
#, js-format
msgid "The listed items are removed, along with their translation records, their string translations and their %d translation job."
msgid_plural "The listed items are removed, along with their translation records, their string translations and their %d translation jobs."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

msgid "We couldn’t check for translated content. You can still remove the language; its translations are kept. Deleting its content and moving it into another language both need that count, so those two goals are unavailable."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Read out to screen readers next to the badge on a choice in the WPML Languages editor; "This" is that choice.
msgid "This can be undone."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Title of a choice in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language name, e.g. "German". Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Stop translating into %s, keep its content online."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %1$s is the language name, e.g. "German", and appears twice in the sentence.
#, js-format
msgid "Your %1$s content stays published at its current addresses and keeps its search rankings. The language switcher keeps offering %1$s."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %1$d: how many translated items there are (posts, pages, categories… — the noun stays neutral), %2$s: the language name, which appears twice in the sentence.
#, js-format
msgid "Your %1$d %2$s item stays published at its current address and keeps its search ranking. The language switcher keeps offering %2$s."
msgid_plural "Your %1$d %2$s items stay published at their current addresses and keep their search rankings. The language switcher keeps offering %2$s."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

msgid "Translations are already paused for this language — nothing more changes."
msgstr ""

msgid "WPML stops creating new translations."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Badge on a choice in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor.
msgid "Nothing is deleted"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Title of a choice in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language name, e.g. "German". Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Take %s off the site, but keep everything in case we come back."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %1$s: the language name, which appears three times in the sentence, %2$s: the site's default language. "404" is the browser's not-found error.
#, js-format
msgid "Visitors stop seeing %1$s; its addresses redirect to your %2$s pages so nothing returns a 404. Everything %1$s holds stays in your database and in your admin lists, and re-adding %1$s brings it back exactly as it was."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %1$s: the language name, which appears twice in the sentence, %2$s: the site's default language, %3$d: how many items there are. "404" is the browser's not-found error.
#, js-format
msgid "Visitors stop seeing %1$s; its addresses redirect to your %2$s pages so nothing returns a 404. The %3$d item stays in your database and in your admin lists, and re-adding %1$s brings it back exactly as it was."
msgid_plural "Visitors stop seeing %1$s; its addresses redirect to your %2$s pages so nothing returns a 404. The %3$d items stay in your database and in your admin lists, and re-adding %1$s brings them back exactly as they were."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: Badge on a choice in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. It says the choice can be undone. Adjective.
msgid "Reversible"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Title of a choice in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language name, e.g. "German". Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Take %s off the site and delete its content."
msgstr ""

msgid "Originals in other languages are untouched. Image files stay on disk."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Badge on the choice that deletes a language's content, in the WPML Languages editor. "the Trash route" is one of the two ways of deleting offered lower in the same dialog.
msgid "Only reversible if the Trash route is chosen"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Badge on the choice that deletes a language's content, in the WPML Languages editor, on a site where WordPress keeps no Trash.
msgid "Not reversible — this site has the Trash disabled"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Read out to screen readers next to the badge on a choice in the WPML Languages editor; "This" is that choice.
msgid "This can only be undone when the items go to the Trash."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Read out to screen readers next to the badge on a choice in the WPML Languages editor, on a site where WordPress keeps no Trash.
msgid "This site has the Trash disabled, so deleting this content cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Title of a choice in the dialog that removes a language, in the WPML Languages editor. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Move this language’s content into another language."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the WPML Languages editor, used when the item count could not be read.
msgid "Reassigns this language’s items to a language you pick, keeping their connections to the other languages. For renaming and merging, not retiring."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Explanation under a choice in the WPML Languages editor. %d: how many items are given to the other language.
#, js-format
msgid "Reassigns the %d item to a language you pick, keeping its connections to the other languages. For renaming and merging, not retiring."
msgid_plural "Reassigns the %d items to a language you pick, keeping their connections to the other languages. For renaming and merging, not retiring."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

msgid "The content is kept, but the move cannot be undone."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Shown in place of the move panel in the WPML Languages editor when the site has no other language to move the content into.
msgid "There is no other active language on this site to move the content into."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Heading of the dialog shown when a language that once existed is added again, in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language name, e.g. "English".
#, js-format
msgid "You have existing content in %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Question under that heading in the WPML Languages editor. %1$d: how many items there are, %2$s: the language name.
#, js-format
msgid "This site has %1$d items in %2$s from before. What should happen to them?"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Radio button in the WPML Languages editor. %1$s: the language name, %2$s: the country, giving e.g. "English (United States)". Verb, imperative.
#, js-format
msgid "Bring back my content as %1$s (%2$s)."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Note under that radio button in the WPML Languages editor. %s: the language code, e.g. "en", which is never translated.
#, js-format
msgid "The language keeps its original code (%s). There is no automatic way back."
msgstr ""

msgid "Start fresh and keep the old content separate."
msgstr ""

msgid "You can attach the old content to the new language later from WPML → Support."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Button label that closes a dialog or a panel without doing anything, in the WPML Languages editor. A gentle way of saying "cancel".
msgid "Never mind"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Button label that confirms adding the language, in the WPML Languages editor. Verb, imperative.
msgid "Add language"
msgstr ""

#. translators: Used in two places in the WPML Languages editor for the same thing: the heading of the dialog that estimates the cost of a new language, and the label of the button that opens it.
msgid "How much would a new language cost?"
msgstr ""

msgid "Pick a language to see how many words your content has and what translating them would cost."
msgstr ""

msgid "These costs apply once you use automatic translation for the new language."
msgstr ""

msgid "No languages are available to estimate. Every language automatic translation supports is already on your site."
msgstr ""

#. translators: Label of the dropdown that picks the language to estimate, in the WPML Languages editor. Noun.
msgid "Language"
msgstr ""

